
      # Why: the cache keeps Mise's installs and downloads but never its shims.
      # A restored shim points at the Mise binary of an earlier run, which Mise
      # treats as unmanaged ("not replacing unmanaged file in shims directory",
      # one warning per tool); Mise regenerates the shims from mise.lock.
      # The key is the content hash of the locks that decide what is
      # installed: one immutable entry per lock state, never one per run, so
      # duplicate generations never consume the repository cache quota.
      # Only that exact key restores. A prefix fallback restored the previous
      # lock state, whose superseded installs and wheels the next save kept:
      # the entry grew with every lock change until its restore filled the
      # runner disk. A lock change
      # installs cold and saves exactly the new state.
      - name: Restore tool caches
        id: tool-cache
        uses: {{ github_actions["cache"].repository }}/restore@{{ github_actions["cache"].version }}
        with:
          path: |
{% include "_fragments/toolchain_cache_paths.j2" %}
          key: {% raw %}${{ runner.os }}-{% endraw %}{{ python_version }}{% raw %}-tools-${{ hashFiles('uv.lock', 'mise.lock', 'pyproject.toml', '.mise.toml') }}{% endraw %}
